// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 4 „Sihitis, ma-/da-infinitiiv ja rektsioon” (b1b2-016…020), stage B1+.
// Methodology v5 „lesson budget” (docs/METHODOLOGY_B1_B2_V5.md, strictModulesV5.json) on the v3 station engine with the
// v4 task formats (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_STATIONS.md §7), built like modules 1–3 (b2/module01.js … module03.js): one real
// communicative outcome a lesson, ONE input, ≤ 4 / 4 / 5 blocks a sheet and ≤ 14 a lesson, a 75-min core in 4 stations.
//   Avasta  (4): station 1 one statement to answer at once (016: the module's cold task, a 1-minute talk without help),
//                station 2 the lesson's words, one explanatory scheme and the ONE input — reading 470–520 words with
//                3 inference questions (016, 018) or listening ~3.5 min with 2 voices and 10 items (017, 019).
//   Harjuta (4): station 3 the rule (the B1 form as a one-line review, then the B2 step), two form tasks of 9–10 items
//                without a word bank (one of them a coherent text) and one register task (spoken → written or
//                official → plain).
//   Kasuta  (5): station 4 the plan, the product (a call to the landlord with hidden information, explaining the school
//                trip to a grandmother with hidden information, a debate with keyword cards, explaining plan B to a
//                grandmother with hidden information), the home writing of ~140 or ~180 words with the 1-min voice
//                message, the analytic Harno B2 rubric (a borderline sample in the teacher's note) and the exit
//                „Ma oskan …” with three success criteria.
//   016 case     „Kas tagatisraha tuleb tagasi?”      home      reading „Kes maksab katkise kapiukse eest?”  object in official use
//   017 infogap  „Mida kool täpselt kirjutas?”        family    call with the class teacher, 2 voices        ma/da in official notices
//   018 debate   „Mille vastu sa huvi tunned?”        freetime  reading „Miks täiskasvanu läheb koori?”      government of nouns and verbs
//   019 project  „Rong jäi ära — mida teha …?”        town      radio talk with a passenger adviser, 2 voices all three in a complaint
//   020 exam     Full B2 mock exam point (v5 §5: B2 020/040/060/080/089/090): Harno B2 form shortened, ≤ 10 blocks a sheet,
//                every recording twice and locked, raw points and thresholds per skill, the module product as speaking 1.
// Module requirements (v5 §2): cold task 016_d_cold (a 1-min talk about a problem the learner had to solve, no phrases)
// ↔ parallel new task 020_t_present (same conditions, the module product „Minu lahendatud mure”); a speech without
// phrases in every station 1; hidden-information cards 016_t_talk, 017_t_talk, 019_t_explain („Varjatud info:”); link
// tasks 018_t_opinion (a real group on vabatahtlikud.ee) and 019_t_letter (the carrier's / TTJA page); one scheme a
// teaching lesson (016 compare, 017 formula, 018 mind, 019 flow); the pictures (art/visuals/b2-module-04.js) stand before
// the input and ask what the input needs; texts are adapted learning texts without exact statistics („KeeleSepp
// õppetekst”, owner 2026-11-25); no story cast, no dictation, no „Kas teadsid?”. The 53-word clip 016_p_done (audit
// 2026-11-25: below B2 as the main input) and the short voice messages left the sheets.
// Kept for the Õpik sheets of 016 (textbook/sihitis.json) and 018 (textbook/minuEesti.json): lesson ids and the goal
// keys g_vocab / g_notice / g_use / g_read.
// Removed blocks stay in the file as hide(block, why) (blocks.js): off every sheet, ids and learners' answers kept; their
// closed drills still feed the Harjuta practice engine (practice/engine/extract.js), with their old explanations.
// The v4 file of 2026-11-17 is in git history (before this commit).
import { B, hide, tag, teach, why, withShapes } from '../blocks.js';
